oup's activity is carried by different members on each side (807/900 before, 923/930 after), which could superficially look like a switch. However, the partner sets are essentially identical: the pre-window contacts of 807 and 900 are exactly the same 30 nodes (18, 61, 189, ..., 1964), and the post-window contacts of 923 and 930 are the same set plus one extra node (1290), giving Jaccard ~0.97 between the old and new contact neighbourhoods. There is no old set of contacts being replaced by a new set; instead a stable contact community is served by rotating group members. Hence no abrupt regime switch of interaction partners.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 14169, "total_output_tokens": 3087, "total_tokens": 17256, "total_latency_ms": 43717, "llm_calls": 4, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}